{"file":"Spec Drift Detector-1.0.0-v2.zip","bytes":124212,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"spec-drift","displayName":"Spec Drift Detector","description":"Detects drift between a session's initial requirements and the final implementation. Extracts a requirement checklist at the start of a task, then compares it against the actual files to report missing, changed, silently-failed, or hardcoded items.","version":"1.0.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/h102-log/spec-drift-detector-plan","homepage":"https://github.com/h102-log/spec-drift-detector-plan","keywords":["spec","drift","requirements","validation","checklist","completion","static-analysis"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/drift-detection/SKILL.md","name":"drift-detection","description":"Compares the requirements recorded in SPEC_CHECKLIST.md against the actual files in the working directory and reports requirement drift. Use whenever a completion is claimed (\"done\", \"finished\", \"implemented\", \"completed\"), when the user asks to verify that a task is really finished, or when auditing whether an implementation still matches what was originally asked for. Classifies each item as missing, changed, silent-fail, hardcode-debt, or done, using read-only static analysis.","headings":["Drift Detection","When to run","Method","Efficient scanning","Scoped detection (`--base <ref>`)","Incremental re-verification (`verified-at`)","Drift classification","Structural verification (Tier 1)","Runtime verification (Tier 2, opt-in)","Drift patterns to watch for","Output: drift report"],"name_hint":"drift · detection","description_zh":"只读静态比较 SPEC_CHECKLIST.md 要求与工作目录实际文件，在声明完成或要求验收时报告偏移，逐项标记缺失、改变、静默失败、硬编码债务或完成。"},{"path":"skills/requirement-extraction/SKILL.md","name":"requirement-extraction","description":"Extracts an explicit requirement checklist from a user's task request and writes it to SPEC_CHECKLIST.md so it can be verified later. Use at the START of a new coding task, whenever a user describes a feature to build, or when the user asks to capture, track, or pin down requirements before implementation begins. Pulls out stated functional requirements plus commonly-forgotten implicit ones (all permission roles, all UI states, all API success/failure paths) and surfaces up to three clarifying questions for genuinely ambiguous scope.","headings":["Requirement Extraction","When to run","Task index maintenance","Task-switch detection","Static and read-only posture","Extraction method","1. Functional requirements (explicit)","2. Implicit requirements (commonly forgotten)","3. Clarifying questions (ambiguous scope only)","Output: SPEC_CHECKLIST.md","Spec Checklist — <ISO timestamp>","Original request","Extracted checklist","Open questions (max 3)","Current implementation status","Closing summary"],"name_hint":"requirement · extraction","description_zh":"在新编码任务开始时提取用户功能要求及易遗漏的权限角色、UI 状态、API 成败路径，写入 SPEC_CHECKLIST.md 供后续验证，最多提出三个真正影响范围的澄清问题。"}],"commands":[{"path":"commands/check.md","name":"check","description":"Show mid-task progress against SPEC_CHECKLIST.md. Runs a fast presence scan of the working directory to estimate how many requirement items are implemented, lists what is still unimplemented, and highlights the ones most at risk of being dropped in the current work context. Use partway through a task for a quick, cheap status read.","headings":["/spec-drift:check","When to use","Options","What it does","Output"]},{"path":"commands/init.md","name":"init","description":"Start a requirement checklist for the current task. Reads the most recent task request, extracts an explicit checklist, and writes SPEC_CHECKLIST.md. Run this at the beginning of a feature or before implementation starts.","headings":["/spec-drift:init","When to use","What it does","Optional argument","Output"]},{"path":"commands/list.md","name":"list","description":"List every spec-drift task (active and archived) with its file and a live done-count read from each checklist. Use to see all concurrent tasks in a project and which one is currently active.","headings":["/spec-drift:list","When to use","What it does","Notes","Output"]},{"path":"commands/report.md","name":"report","description":"Generate a full drift report comparing SPEC_CHECKLIST.md against the actual files, then feed the result back as corrective guidance. Run this when a completion is claimed or when you want to audit whether the implementation matches the original requirements.","headings":["/spec-drift:report","When to use","Options","Incremental re-verification","What it does","Output"]},{"path":"commands/switch.md","name":"switch","description":"Switch the active spec-drift task: archive the current SPEC_CHECKLIST.md and promote an archived SPEC_CHECKLIST.<slug>.md to active, updating the index. Never overwrites silently.","headings":["/spec-drift:switch","When to use","Argument","What it does","Notes","Output"]}],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Spec Drift Detector","How it works","Installation","Local install (current)","From the community marketplace (after publishing)","Commands","`/spec-drift:init`","`/spec-drift:check`","`/spec-drift:report`","`/spec-drift:list`","`/spec-drift:switch`","Skills (model-invoked)","Example","`SPEC_CHECKLIST.md` produced by `/spec-drift:init`","Spec Checklist — 2026-06-24T14:32:00","Original request","Extracted checklist","Open questions (max 3)","Current implementation status","Drift report produced by `/spec-drift:report`","Security","Benchmarks — does it actually help?","Where it helps (and where it doesn't)","Limitations","Committing the checklist","Continuous integration (optional)","Contributing","License"]},{"path":"test-fixtures/README.md","headings":["Test Fixtures (development only)","`sample-project/`","How to run T5","How to run T6","`complex-project/`","`adversarial-project/`","`crossfile-project/`","`async-project/`","`indirection-project/`","`trick-project/`"]},{"path":"skills/drift-detection/ru